 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532930,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the measures of the unknown sides in the given figure.\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/bf462e163a2bcafe.png\" alt=\"A right triangle, A B C. The legs, C A, and A B measure x and x. The hypotenuse, C B measures 8. The angles, C and B are congruent. Angle A is a right angle.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The set of ratios in a 45°-45°-90° triangle are <span data-math=\"1:1:\\sqrt 2 \"></span>, or <span data-math=\"x:x:x\\sqrt 2 \"></span>.</p>\n<p>They show the 90° angle and two other angles of equal measure. That means the other two angles have a measure of 45° each.</p>\n<p>Since 8 is the longest side,  <span data-math=\"8 = x\\sqrt 2 \"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = \\frac{8}{{\\sqrt 2 }}\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = \\frac{8}{{\\sqrt 2 }}\\left( {\\frac{{\\sqrt 2 }}{{\\sqrt 2 }}} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Rationalize the denominator.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = \\frac{{8\\sqrt 2 }}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = 4\\sqrt 2 \"></span> or approximately 5.66.</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Each side <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> equals <span data-math=\"x = 4\\sqrt 2 = 5.66.\">x = 4\\sqrt 2 = 5.66.</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
